# §0. Statements

Let f be the planar 3D Bargmann–Fock field or the normalized periodized
side-24 field; pins V = (f, ∇f)(M), (f, ∇f)(S), S − M = (d,0,0), d > 0;
y = M + ρu, |u| = 1; Γ_d(u) = Cov(Hf(M)u | V) (the corrected G.9.1 object,
cross-line exact); C(ρ) = Cov(∇f(y) | V).

**Lemma 1 (additive ρ-remainder, uniform over ALL strata).** There are
constants ρ₀ > 0 and c₁ < ∞, depending only on unconditional second/third
derivative moments of the field, such that for all d > 0, all |u| = 1, all
0 < ρ ≤ ρ₀:

|det C(ρ)/ρ⁶ − det Γ_d(u)| ≤ c₁ ρ.

**Lemma 2 (row-weighted refinement).** With G_i(ρ) the components of
∫₀¹ H(M+tρu)u dt and c₂ = sup unconditional second moments of
D³f[u,u,·]-integrands,

|det C(ρ)/ρ⁶ − det Γ_d(u)|
≤ 3ρ √c₂ · max_i √(Γ_d(u)_{ii}) · ‖adj Γ_d(u)‖_row + O(ρ²),

i.e. the perturbation of row i is bounded by ρ√c₂·√(Γ_ii): **the
first-order error inherits half the degeneracy of each row of Γ.**

**Corollary (axial relative window).** On the axis u = e₁, where
Γ ≈ diag(d⁴/6, d²/2, d²/2) and det Γ ≈ d⁸/24: row 1's replacement
contributes ≤ ρ·O(d²)·(d²/2)² = O(ρ d⁶) and rows 2–3 contribute O(ρ d⁷),
so

det C(ρ)/ρ⁶ = det Γ_d(e₁) · (1 + O(ρ/d²)).

**Two-sided determinant control therefore holds whenever ρ ≤ ε d² — not
merely ρ ≲ d⁸-class — and the axial Gaussian suppression (residual item 2)
need only absorb the region ρ ≳ ε d², which its e^{−c/r²}-class factor
does with room to spare.** This is the sharpening of G.9.x residual
item (1).

# §1. Proof of Lemma 1

On the pin event ∇f(M) = 0 exactly, so pathwise (smooth field, a.s.):

∇f(M+ρu) = ρ ∫₀¹ H(M+tρu)u dt =: ρ G(ρ),

hence C(ρ)/ρ² = Cov(G(ρ) | V) with G(0) = Hf(M)u, so
C(0⁺)/ρ² → Γ_d(u) entrywise. The conditioning σ-algebra is **fixed** (does
not move with ρ), so ∂_ρ Cov(G_i, G_j | V) = Cov(G_i′, G_j | V) +
Cov(G_i, G_j′ | V), with G′(ρ) = ∫₀¹ t·D³f(M+tρu)[u,u,·] dt. By
conditional Cauchy–Schwarz and Var(· | V) ≤ Var(·):

|∂_ρ [C/ρ²]_ij| ≤ 2 √(E G_i′²) √(E G_j²) ≤ 2√(c₂ c₀) =: L,

**uniformly in (ρ, d, u)** — the pins never enter the bound. Entries of
C/ρ² are likewise ≤ c₀ uniformly. The mean-value theorem gives entrywise
|[C/ρ²]_ij − Γ_ij| ≤ Lρ, and for 3×3 matrices with entries bounded by c₀,
|det A − det B| ≤ 18 c₀² ‖A−B‖_∞. Take c₁ = 18 c₀² L. For the periodized
field the identical proof runs with its own (finite, nearby) moment
constants; by the G.9.2 transfer those differ from planar by < 10⁻¹⁰⁰ on
the collar range. ∎

# §2. Proof of Lemma 2 and the corollary

Row i of the first-order perturbation is Cov(G_i′, G_j | V) +
Cov(G_i, G_j′ | V); conditional Cauchy–Schwarz bounds the **second** term
by √(Var(G_i|V))·√(Var(G_j′|V)) ≤ √(Γ_ii)·√c₂ — the row inherits √Γ_ii.
(The first term is bounded the same way with the roles of i, j exchanged;
collecting both keeps the max_i √Γ_ii weight.) Expanding det(Γ + ρP) − 
det Γ row-by-row (multilinearity), each single-row replacement is ≤
‖P_i‖·‖adj row‖, giving Lemma 2. On the axis: Var(f_xx|V) = d⁴/6 + O(d⁶)
(verified §5), Var(f_xy|V) = Var(f_xz|V) = d²/2 + O(d⁴), cross terms zero
(the corrected G.9.1 diagonal structure), so the minors and weights
evaluate to the displayed d-powers and det Γ ≈ d⁸/24. ∎

